Subject: [PATCH] Re-land the eleven review fixes the #229 squash left behind
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PR #229 was squash-merged from a point three commits before the branch
tip, so `main` has the WO-AH work, the evidence gate, the six report
defects and the intent matrix — but not the review round that followed.
Four of the missing fixes are P1, and all four are live defects on main
right now:

- Pressing Cancel on a run freezes the user's wallet money for thirty
  minutes. The button this PR series added has no hold release behind it.
- A run queued with the removed "Devil's Advocate" add-on is charged $5
  for a stronger challenge pass that never runs.
- The scaled source budget computes a number nothing uses: discovery
  still takes `min(planner's request, cap)`, so the "only 9 sources"
  complaint is not actually fixed on main.
- The relevance filter classifies sources as off-topic and then ingests
  them anyway to fill the cap, so the "why are these sources here"
  complaint is not actually fixed either.

Two more are regressions #229 itself introduced and shipped:

- `stripLeadingOrdinal` turns `ISO 27001: Security controls` into
  `Security controls` — the fix for corrupted headings corrupting them.
- `stripLeadingSectionHeading` deletes the label from any section that
  opens with `### Risks`.

The rest: a failed billing lookup silently downgrading a paid user to
free, a second prefill carrying the previous request's settings, an
over-broad opportunity trigger stealing explicit comparison requests,
five screens still advertising "Deep Research", and `/docs` still saying
"skeptic" while outside the jargon manifest.

No new work. This is the content of `cursor/one-research-system` that
`main` does not have, applied unchanged, with the tests and the
mutation evidence that came with each fix.

Gates: backend 1581 pass, frontend 362 pass, typecheck and lint clean
both sides, Tier A check passes on 20 files.

